              "source": "PubMed"
            },
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "id": "30560135",
              "source": "PubMed"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Viable, with no gross anatomy or growth defects observed (PubMed:22916205). Localization of aat-6 at the intestinal apical cell membrane diminishes as animals age, and eventually aat-6 becomes diffusely dispersed in the cytoplasm (PubMed:22916205). RNAi-mediated knockdown in a pept-1 (lg601) mutant background results in a reduced number of progeny (PubMed:30560135)"
        }
      ]
    }
